  "context": "0411.colab designs a Colab support module. Its section on compute proposes five operations: prepare, verify, intake, review and find. The first implementation (0510.colab-tools/05.02) builds prepare, verify and intake only. Review and find are not built. Prime will use the tool on real work before a fresh Colab probes it.",
  "question": "Do the five proposed operations divide deterministic compute work from intelligence work at the right places, and which operation boundary is most likely to make Prime repeat manual work or lose a finding?",
  "why": "If the split is wrong, the module either automates a judgement it should only record, or leaves Prime re-typing context and custody facts on every Colab. Both failures were seen before the design was recovered.",
  "built_state": "prepare, verify and intake exist as lab code that wraps the accepted pack assembler, custody checker, return capture helper and inspector. review and find exist only as the design text in the target section.",
  "known_gaps": [
    "No investigation member exists in 0700.band.colabs yet; this binding names a declared fixture page.",
    "The workflow adapter that attaches a package to an investigation pass is being built separately and is not part of this package.",
    "Section ids have no declared syntax in interface v1, so only exact headings can select a section."
  ],
  "method": "Read the target section first, then the interface contract and the record groups. For each operation, say what input it needs, what it may decide by itself, and what it must leave to Prime or the Director. You may propose a different split or a different first slice if you can show why.",
  "cases": [
    {
      "id": "C01",
      "text": "A return arrives with a Hostile finding that contradicts a Director decision. Walk it through intake, review and find. Where could it be lost or silently promoted?"
    },
    {
      "id": "C02",
      "text": "Prime wants to reuse a prior experiment on the same subject page. Which operation must expose that, and from what record?"
    },
    {
      "id": "C03",
      "text": "A package is prepared for a ZIP-only recipient, and one required source is an image that was never committed. Which operation should stop it, and with what message?"
    }
